{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1151619-monotheism-and-henotheism","id":1151619,"title":"Monotheism and Henotheism","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-21T04:52:27-07:00","id":1151619,"title":"Monotheism and Henotheism","content":"So, given that the existence of the gods is fairly widely acknowledged, what is the official stance of the monotheistic faiths? I'm curious about this because pre-rabbinical Judaism appears to have been henotheistic rather than purely monotheistic. How does the presence of active gods change the evolution of Judaism and, later, Christianity and Islam?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1583-the-insaniac","name":"The Insaniac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T08:12:40-07:00","id":1151644,"title":"","content":"My pure speculation right now is the continuous survival of European polytheistic worship in the Word does indicate a less aggressively monotheistic form of Christianity, that didn\u2019t require the rejection of the Theoi, Aesir, Tuatha, etc - just the acceptance of Christ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T11:54:58-07:00","id":1151701,"title":"","content":"My default assumption would be that the God of Judaism, Christianity, and Islam is a primordial, and the followers of those faiths believe that the other pantheons, though divine and mighty in their own right, are ultimately pretenders on par with the mightiest members of the heavenly host. Not that that makes it true in the World, but it's the views of those particular faiths. It preserves both the real history of those faiths overshadowing the others, but still leaves room for them not to try and convert entire belief systems, since in the end they're still technically serving the almighty through his servants like Ra and Odin. Again, not saying this is the truth of the setting, just the rational of people that worship that deity in setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T12:17:24-07:00","id":1151705,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m trying to decide for my own table whether there should be a separate Mal\u2019akhim Pantheon that the Primordial El created who are more unwaveringly loyal to Him than His blood descended deities in the Elohim Pantheon (the Canaanite/Phoenician/Carthaginian gods).<br /> <br /> I had the idea in 1E to pull on Judaic apocrypha and have the Mal\u2019akhim refer to all other divinities as \u201cGrigori\u201d, and all Scions as\u201dNephilim\u201d. They were forbidden to create Nephilim of their own, but they could adopt Jewish, Christian, and Muslim Nephilim who rejected their birth Pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T14:17:40-07:00","id":1151748,"title":"","content":"Easy: the other gods exist, they\u2019re just either your pick of demons or not worthy of worship before God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-21T19:28:41-07:00","id":1151818,"title":"","content":"Since Christianity and Islam kept a lot of knowledge alive, i'm more curious how thier absence or alteration would have affected that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 10-22-2017, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T09:26:24-07:00","id":1152215,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar490_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"490\" data-vbnamecard=\"490\">omenseer</a>; well, without the presence of actual gods there probably would have been even less record of oral tradition religions, leading to further decline until they're finally lost to history forever. Of course, we're assuming the presence of actual divine powers so I'd imagine they'd send a prophet/scion periodically to restore knowledge of the old ways. That is, unless they really don't want any worshipers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T10:30:17-07:00","id":1152226,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about the three names of the One God above the Orisha (Olorun, Olodumare, and Olofin), and how from a Christian synchronistic perspective that obviously fits with the Holy Trinity. They'd probably see the Three Pure Ones of the Shen, and Zoka shansin of the Kami as faces of the same Primordial whole. While Vishnu and Shiva chose to engage on the God rather than Primordial level, the Trimurti follow the same pattern, even while the Tridevi bring an equal feminine aspect to the equation. And the Deva in turn, looking at the Elohim would see the Primordials El and Asherah as aspects of Brahmin and Shakti the same way! And then you start looking at Kitchi Manitou and Wakan Tanka...<br /> <br /> Of course not every Pantheon is going to be on board with this kind of talk:<br /> <br /> The most vehemently opposed would be the Netjer, who see Aten lurking behind every hint of Monism or Supreme-Creator-Henotheism (whether he's actually involved or not).<br /> <br /> The Theoi aren't threatened by the notion of a Prime Mover preceding the Olympians, they know damn well generations of Titans and Primordials preceded the gods - but that doesn't make said hypothetical Prime Mover a higher being above the Throne of Zeus. The Olympians take pride in having brought primordial cosmic predecessors to heel into THEIR ORDER, so such conversations are recreational philosophy at best, not religion. The fact that other Pantheons would honor such (a) being/s as above themselves means they allow themselves to be dominated where the Olympians took the greatest power for themselves.<br /> <br /> And then the Aesir just sigh with knowing sadness, as any such higher power is obviously just personification imposed on the cruel unflinching Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-23-2017, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T20:23:42-07:00","id":1153375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1151619-monotheism-and-henotheism?p=1151705#post1151705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m trying to decide for my own table whether there should be a separate Mal\u2019akhim Pantheon that the Primordial El created who are more unwaveringly loyal to Him than His blood descended deities in the Elohim Pantheon (the Canaanite/Phoenician/Carthaginian gods).<br /> <br /> I had the idea in 1E to pull on Judaic apocrypha and have the Mal\u2019akhim refer to all other divinities as \u201cGrigori\u201d, and all Scions as\u201dNephilim\u201d. They were forbidden to create Nephilim of their own, but they could adopt Jewish, Christian, and Muslim Nephilim who rejected their birth Pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd play a game that included either/both of those pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T22:27:56-07:00","id":1154296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1151619-monotheism-and-henotheism?p=1151701#post1151701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My default assumption would be that the God of Judaism, Christianity, and Islam is a primordial, and the followers of those faiths believe that the other pantheons, though divine and mighty in their own right, are ultimately pretenders on par with the mightiest members of the heavenly host. Not that that makes it true in the World, but it's the views of those particular faiths. It preserves both the real history of those faiths overshadowing the others, but still leaves room for them not to try and convert entire belief systems, since in the end they're still technically serving the almighty through his servants like Ra and Odin. Again, not saying this is the truth of the setting, just the rational of people that worship that deity in setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's kind of what they were going for in 1E. It's pretty obvious that Aten is supposed to be an allegory for the Abrahamic God in his most power hungry representation. Suicide bombers, an army of angels, and outright refusing to allow any other Avatars of Light exist are all pretty hard to ignore.<br /> <br /> As I understand it, monotheism came about in Judaism by gradually interpreting their pantheon as different avatars of the same divine being. Which, if you look at it from that perspective, makes a lot of his contradictory actions make more sense. He was probably acting under a different avatar at the time, but the act was associated with same person.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also a pre-made antagonist group that tries to replicate this process with all deities, manipulating the perceptions of mortal society and their connection with Fate to absorb all Gods into a single, omnipotent being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-31-2017, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T04:35:06-07:00","id":1154336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1151619-monotheism-and-henotheism?p=1154296#post1154296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand it, monotheism came about in Judaism by gradually interpreting their pantheon as different avatars of the same divine being. Which, if you look at it from that perspective, makes a lot of his contradictory actions make more sense. He was probably acting under a different avatar at the time, but the act was associated with same person.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t believe so. Judaism\u2019s route to monotheism was more henotheistic than monistic. It was more that there was only one God who got any attention. Others got excluded, demonized, or maybe reduced to angels.<br /> <br /> The only thing I can think of that kind of plays into a monistic evolution narrative is how the plural Elohim came to be applied to the singular G-d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T12:46:05-07:00","id":1154475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1151619-monotheism-and-henotheism?p=1154336#post1154336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t believe so. Judaism\u2019s route to monotheism was more henotheistic than monistic. It was more that there was only one God who got any attention. Others got excluded, demonized, or maybe reduced to angels.<br /> <br /> The only thing I can think of that kind of plays into a monistic evolution narrative is how the plural Elohim came to be applied to the singular G-d.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, in my bible lessons in high school, my teacher has supported the monistic view toward Judaism, and it is the most common view in here for non religious jews who discuss the evolution of Judaism (and in here, I mean Israel).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T14:39:51-07:00","id":1154516,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll have to read more on the subject then. I know there is certainly \u201cthey shall become like us\u201d passage, but I wasn\u2019t aware of more solid historic evidence of multiple deities being treated as aspects of YHWH.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T21:02:07-07:00","id":1154974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1151619-monotheism-and-henotheism?p=1154516#post1154516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll have to read more on the subject then. I know there is certainly \u201cthey shall become like us\u201d passage, but I wasn\u2019t aware of more solid historic evidence of multiple deities being treated as aspects of YHWH.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MlnnWbkMlbg\" target=\"_blank\">A History of God</a><br /> <br /> Warning, probably shouldn't watch if you're easily offended by matters of theology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-02-2017, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T08:49:41-08:00","id":1159875,"title":"","content":"For Christianity, I think there is one change that would have a lot of useful consequences. Namely, the Bishop of Rome does not end up becoming more important than other bishops. Western Europe ends up more like the Orthodox - the most authority is one bishop being the leader of a handful of bishoprics. In effect you have a Roman Orthodox, Paris Orthodox, Scottish Orthodox, etc. <br /> <br /> So, consequences. Churches are much more local, and there is no Papal force laying down a single viewpoint. You can still have Irish monks preserving lore (IIRC, the Irish were practically their own sect before the English church went over there. I think circa 1100's? Not sure). Attitudes towards other gods will depend much more on the locale. Sure, the bishop in Sweden accepts that the Norse gods are real. Not as powerful as our god, but real. Meanwhile, the Bavarian church has tried to wipe out all mention of any other gods, Irish church recognizes different ones, etc etc<br /> <br /> I would also run with the ideas of &quot;conversion by explaining how their gods are part of our religion&quot; and &quot;saints as culture heros&quot; Odin hanging from a tree? That is totally a version of the Jesus story. Thor, big guy with hammer? Oh, he's St Christopher. <br /> <br /> If I explained this right, the end result would be a very diverse, mostly henotheistic christianity, with a &quot;Pantheon&quot; of saints. Some would be gods of other Pantheons under a different name, some would be hero-types. Not sure where angels would fall in all this. The actual local pantheon and their views on other pantheons would vary a lot and allow for pro and anti-factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T12:45:00-08:00","id":1159977,"title":"","content":"If the Bishop of Rome wasn't placed over other bishops in the West, would the schism with the Orthodox Church even have happened?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T13:16:43-08:00","id":1159990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1151619-monotheism-and-henotheism?p=1154974#post1154974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MlnnWbkMlbg\" target=\"_blank\">A History of God</a><br /> <br /> Warning, probably shouldn't watch if you're easily offended by matters of theology.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's consistent with what I've studied. It was a henotheistic trend that grew into monotheism. There is, in this video's version the possibly conflation of originally separate deities El Elyon and Yahweh Sabaoth, though I'm not aware of evidence outside the Bible of Yahweh Sabaoth having been a distinct war god in the region from El, and I know some scholars believe Yahweh was always an epithet of El. Still the overall trend in the &quot;History of God&quot; narrative is one of exclusionary henotheism, not assimilationist monotheism. Ba'al Hadad, Anat, Asherah, Dagon, etc were rejected by the cult of YHWH, not assimilated as aspects of Him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}